  "gloss": "name, renown, there",
  "id": "shem",
  "note": "Arabic thamma distinguishes the historical initial consonant of there from that of name. The proper names have different degrees of transparency. Hannah herself explains Samuel’s name by her asking Yahweh for him.",
  "root": "שמ",
  "status": "draft",
  "summary": "A name identifies someone and can preserve their memory. In the Psalms, loving or praising Yahweh’s name expresses devotion to Yahweh himself. The consonants also write a place adverb distinguished by its vowel and its cognates.",
  "tags": [
    "names",
    "worship",
    "memory",
    "place"
  ],
